{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"Cargo.toml","issuer":"mailto:claude-review@anthropic.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-05-06T21:04:09.856919Z","id":"ccfe88fa371549c80feff4d15e6cd0db767a7c428b4b12f7d9750c0f7bd5060c","body":{"detail":"Cargo.toml lists petgraph = \"0.7\" but no source file imports it: 'grep -rn petgraph src tests' returns nothing. The dependency was added for src/graph.rs (DependencyGraph, toposort, cycle detection), which was yanked in the same wave as scoring. Carrying it inflates build times and the binary size for no gain.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":24},"end":{"line":24},"content_hash":"bab5a998dd0d510c555f7bc68c7296f6068164a3305155a633cc11fd62f102da"},"suggested_fix":"Remove the petgraph entry from [dependencies]. If you anticipate bringing the graph engine back per SPEC §12 Future Considerations, leave a brief commit-message note rather than a dead dep — re-adding the line is cheap.","summary":"petgraph dependency is unused after the graph engine yank","tags":["review","cleanup"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"Cargo.toml","issuer":"mailto:alex@empathic.dev","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-05-08T03:15:18.383650Z","id":"23e83817b9194995f38452eb705bb1c3f5253b0f991f01c1c203d21929b92ae2","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"petgraph removed from Cargo.toml","supersedes":"ccfe88fa371549c80feff4d15e6cd0db767a7c428b4b12f7d9750c0f7bd5060c"}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"SPEC.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:18:11.952415Z","id":"dcef24fc5e4781e5f101194d51e856c5b59365e948811a1ad1e98e4a6120713c","body":{"detail":"SPEC.md §6.10 says `issuer` and `format` resolve from CLI flag, env var, `.qualifier.toml`, then `~/.config/qualifier/config.toml`, with `QUALIFIER_FORMAT` as the env var for format. In src/cli/mod.rs:118-126 `config::load` is called only to surface parse errors and its result is discarded (the comment says 'no command consumes Config yet'). Every command's `--format` is a clap default of `human` with no env binding, and issuer resolution in src/cli/provenance.rs reads only `--issuer`, `QUALIFIER_ISSUER`, the harness and VCS identity. So `issuer = \"mailto:me@example.com\"` in `.qualifier.toml` and `QUALIFIER_FORMAT=json` are silently ignored. SPEC.md §8.4 (issuer: flag, env, harness, VCS; no config file) already contradicts §6.10. site/pages/cli.md:180-190 repeats the same table.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1196},"end":{"line":1213},"content_hash":"6aca8a925fe03259ac2a9eefabf368abf73c1b0bbd7e3296021ae25d2c3cf039"},"suggested_fix":"Either wire Config into issuer resolution and the `--format` default, or rewrite SPEC §6.10 and site/pages/cli.md 'Configuration' to say config files are parsed for validity only and list the env vars that actually work (QUALIFIER_ISSUER, QUALIFIER_ISSUER_TYPE, QUALIFIER_SESSION), pointing at §8.4.","summary":"SPEC §6.10 documents layered config (.qualifier.toml, user config, QUALIFIER_FORMAT) that no command consumes","tags":["review","review:2026-10-01","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"SPEC.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:18:11.952481Z","id":"7bc642e3d8a87d900f71723f8b2573905e646b2834dc47e15ed45618f86cbd59","body":{"detail":"SPEC.md §6.6 says 'Use `--line <n>` to filter to annotations overlapping a specific line' and '`--pretty` forces colored output when piped'. `qualifier show src/x.rs --line 60` fails with clap 'unexpected argument --line found'; src/cli/commands/show.rs Args has no line option. `--pretty` actually prints source context around each span (compiler-diagnostic style) and, with `--format json`, adds a `context` field (show.rs:74-96, 170-183); it does not control color. The existing `--type <TYPE>` filter is not mentioned. site/pages/cli.md:108 repeats the `--pretty` color claim.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1144},"end":{"line":1150},"content_hash":"5035d7eb3e6cc3c35f98fa812ecdd64d6661e21bf62c545d302d4d311f30f933"},"suggested_fix":"Delete the `--line` sentence (or point at `qualifier threads path:line`), describe `--pretty` as 'show source context around spans', and document `--type <TYPE>`; make the same edit in site/pages/cli.md:108.","summary":"SPEC §6.6 documents a `show --line` flag that does not exist and misdescribes `--pretty`","tags":["review","review:2026-10-01","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"SPEC.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:18:11.952535Z","id":"1ae0014cdd5ab2f285220d8d205a1f4bb731a546a0cce236f8670d486d45e375","body":{"detail":"`qualifier --help` (src/cli/mod.rs HELP_TEMPLATE and the Commands enum) lists init, agents, diff, and haiku in addition to the commands in SPEC.md §6.1. `qualifier diff [ref]` (src/cli/commands/diff.rs: --format, --from-tip, --fail-on, --fail-on-drift, --kind, --issuer-type, --subjects-only, --no-ignore) has no SPEC section at all, although it has its own `qualifier agents diff` page and CI-gating exit-code semantics. `init` is only mentioned in passing in §8.2 and `agents` only in §9. SPEC.md §11 Crate Structure likewise lists none of commands/{agents,diff,init,threads}.rs.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":901},"end":{"line":927},"content_hash":"682fe0440acfbb55615e8e29567f037562bc65ef2253c2c3c06c6c3f581699bc"},"suggested_fix":"Add `qualifier init`, `qualifier agents [topic]` and `qualifier diff [ref]` to the §6.1 command blocks and add a §6.x section for `diff` describing its buckets (added, resolved, drifted), merge-base default, `--fail-on`/`--fail-on-drift` exit codes and JSON shape.","summary":"SPEC §6 omits the shipped `qualifier diff`, `init`, and `agents` commands","tags":["review","review:2026-10-01","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"README.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:18:11.952570Z","id":"ef6c9f07a9b19d012648a1d9cf35ff94236e3f396dfb134163592870e8fcb77b","body":{"detail":"README.md 'Inspect annotations' lists show, threads, ls, praise and review, but `qualifier --help` also groups `diff` ('Show records added, resolved, or drifted since a git ref') under Inspect annotations (src/cli/mod.rs HELP_TEMPLATE). AGENTS.md 'Keeping Things in Sync' requires the README CLI Commands table to reflect current behavior.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":77},"end":{"line":93},"content_hash":"bbbf75c61cacc041ac442347bfd7e18eae4fac8bf38825d141f07c959ded5527"},"suggested_fix":"Add a row: `qualifier diff [ref]` | Show records added, resolved, or drifted since a git ref (merge-base with `main` by default).","summary":"README CLI tables omit `qualifier diff`","tags":["review","review:2026-10-01","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"SPEC.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:18:11.952664Z","id":"e7a94f7b4e0d9fd5a251d067234f7a5560f2c5af662d80a9650abfebbb762cbc","body":{"detail":"SPEC.md §7 says to add `qualifier = { version = \"0.4\", default-features = false }`. Under Cargo semver for 0.x, \"0.4\" resolves to >=0.4.0,<0.5.0, so consumers get a crate without `qualifier::threads` (documented in the same section, added in 0.8.0) and with pre-0.8 supersession semantics. Cargo.toml is at 0.8.0. SPEC.md §12 similarly says its items are 'not part of v0.3'.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1270},"end":{"line":1274},"content_hash":"13f97ca66abc2ae5d23d4af8ef396fc489ee1324d3db235ec46efee398e6d8d5"},"suggested_fix":"Change the snippet to `version = \"0.8\"` and update it whenever the minor version is bumped (or write `version = \"<current minor>\"` with a note); change §12 to 'not part of the current release'.","summary":"SPEC §7 tells library consumers to depend on qualifier 0.4, which lacks the API the section documents","tags":["review","review:2026-10-01","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"SPEC.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:18:11.952720Z","id":"0911ef53b6165da15bedfb53a341b7b48475db5418b3e88e8ab46d4eb2826def","body":{"detail":"AGENTS.md requires SPEC §7 to match public function signatures. Public items missing from §7: qual_file::{parse_str, write_all, resolve_qual_path, find_records_for, find_annotations_for, find_qual_file_for, subject_name, find_project_root, detect_vcs} (src/qual_file.rs:46-274); annotation::{parse_span, parse_location, check_supersession_cycles, validate_supersession_targets} and Record::record_type, Span::{end_or_start, normalize} (src/annotation.rs); and the crate-level `Error`/`Result` types in src/lib.rs that every listed function returns. `write_all` is what compaction and any library writer need, and `check_supersession_cycles` enforces a SPEC §2.9 MUST, so a consumer reading §7 cannot find them.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1376},"end":{"line":1391},"content_hash":"378c01ffe58c3c5d4f8a71dcfa3a11599d015e21776131993fd697d4145c05f0"},"suggested_fix":"List the missing public functions in §7 with their signatures, or mark the internal ones `pub(crate)` / `#[doc(hidden)]` and state that §7 is the supported subset.","summary":"SPEC §7 Library API omits much of the public surface of qual_file and annotation","tags":["review","review:2026-10-01","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"SPEC.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:18:11.952770Z","id":"b7039ad28d4f9015640a2c84aa83ed2a6107685862d42e9fc6b8c5ee33170dc6","body":{"detail":"SPEC.md §2.8.1 rule 3 and METABOX.md §3.2 say nested objects (like `span`) have keys in lexicographic order, which would be content_hash, end, start. `Span` in src/annotation.rs:22-31 declares start, end, content_hash, and generate_id serializes the struct directly, so qualifier hashes `\"span\":{\"start\":...,\"end\":...,\"content_hash\":...}` (confirmed in a freshly recorded .qual line). SPEC.md §2.8.2 example (line 449) also shows start before end. An independent implementation that follows the written rule computes a different ID for every span-addressed record, defeating cross-implementation content addressing (METABOX.md §4). The MCF also does not define a canonical `created_at` string: qualifier hashes chrono's re-serialization (e.g. a stored `2026-02-24T10:00:00.000Z` hashes as `2026-02-24T10:00:00Z`), which another implementation cannot reproduce from the text alone.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":416},"end":{"line":418},"content_hash":"eaaf34e3e28a1dd211d3303b5d701697e56c89846fc2dcb17bff9bd19dfd3e25"},"suggested_fix":"Decide which is normative. Either reorder Span fields alphabetically (content_hash, end, start — changes IDs, so bump the spec version and update golden IDs) or amend rule 3 to exempt span with an explicit start, end, content_hash order and fix METABOX §3.2. Also specify the canonical timestamp form (e.g. RFC 3339 UTC with `Z`, fractional seconds only when non-zero, as chrono emits).","summary":"MCF rule says nested objects are key-sorted, but span serializes start/end/content_hash and the spec's own example follows that order","tags":["review","review:2026-10-01","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"SPEC.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:18:11.952823Z","id":"9c7f30d62c7a9a4334ffaea04d862cbc0fc8f3f1a9247caa43285151ae2c3461","body":{"detail":"src/qual_file.rs discover() uses ignore::WalkBuilder with its default require_git(true), so `.gitignore` rules apply only when a `.git` directory exists (see https://docs.rs/ignore/latest/ignore/struct.WalkBuilder.html#method.require_git). In a Mercurial project (`.hg` root) with `.gitignore` containing `vendor/`, `qualifier ls` still lists records from vendor/.qual; renaming `.hg` to `.git` hides them (reproduced with 0.8.0). WalkBuilder's default ignore(true) also honors `.ignore` files, which §10.1 does not mention. The list of affected commands (show, ls, compact, review, praise) also omits threads, diff, and reply/resolve ID-prefix lookup, which use the same discovery. README.md:131 repeats the unconditional claim.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1514},"end":{"line":1533},"content_hash":"a1f5554d684e640b17eec51cc9e9fbbee53c3ca1d234a5b3fe9ad9b3a1f27443"},"suggested_fix":"Either call `builder.require_git(false)` in discover() so `.gitignore` applies in every VCS (and decide whether `.ignore` should be honored), or document both behaviors in §10.1 and README. Update the command list to 'all commands that discover .qual files'.","summary":"§10.1 says .gitignore is always honored, but outside a git repo it is ignored, and `.ignore` files are honored undocumented","tags":["review","review:2026-10-01","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"SPEC.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:18:11.952871Z","id":"81f88ec84b199e644c33fda7e353ec00506546c418cc94856939d1b468c9fda8","body":{"detail":"SPEC.md §2.4.3 (lines 259-261) says content_hash is computed 'via flag, suggest, comment, approve, reject, attest --span' — commands removed in 0.4.0 (CHANGELOG.md [0.4.0] Removed); the writers are now record, reply, resolve. §2.7.1 line 384 says 'see Appendix A' but there is no appendix; the scoring example is §4. §2.11 line 565 says 'the original concern's -10 is withdrawn from scoring', but the format carries no score since 0.4.0.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":259},"end":{"line":263},"content_hash":"efda0ef46abfcb295b21ca611c28a41e30d38c79a425a9a7aeb263b898cba25c"},"suggested_fix":"Replace the command list with '`record`, `reply`, `resolve`, and `record --stdin`'; change 'Appendix A' to '§4'; reword line 565 to 'After the resolve, the original concern leaves the active set; the reply remains visible in the thread for context.'","summary":"SPEC still refers to removed commands, scoring, and a nonexistent Appendix A","tags":["review","review:2026-10-01","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"SPEC.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:18:11.952926Z","id":"2e6daa85403292cd2efaf740290456ea56ad1521e935f43795a3b94b9cdf9bbd","body":{"detail":"§11 omits src/threads.rs (public module `qualifier::threads`), src/cli/{provenance,targets}.rs, and src/cli/commands/{agents/,diff,init,threads}.rs, and its `[features]` block shows `cli = [\"dep:clap\", \"dep:comfy-table\", \"dep:figment\"]` while Cargo.toml:18 also gates dep:gix, dep:globset and dep:rand.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":1556},"end":{"line":1596},"content_hash":"409bb725eee2c45f7db324802e2bfba0cff2e9526ba41dec8204165d7092c59a"},"suggested_fix":"Regenerate the tree from `src/` and copy the `[features]` block from Cargo.toml.","summary":"SPEC §11 Crate Structure and features list are out of date","tags":["review","review:2026-10-01","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"CHANGELOG.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:18:11.952965Z","id":"044147bd254d7992c047ad9c98bf8c5aeaf1fe908493605060ae4d5249176626","body":{"detail":"`qualifier diff` and its flags (--from-tip, --fail-on, --fail-on-drift, --kind, --issuer-type, --subjects-only) shipped in commit a6f6813, when Cargo.toml was at 0.5.1, but no CHANGELOG entry ([0.5.1] or elsewhere) records it, so a reader of release notes cannot learn the command exists or when it appeared.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":127},"end":{"line":147},"content_hash":"59479d52068c75fca0f65d9f31461d14cbc601b93ab6493d91b7c8ce36c5cb1d"},"suggested_fix":"Add under [0.5.1] Added: '`qualifier diff [ref]` — records added, resolved, or drifted since a git ref (merge-base by default); `--fail-on KIND` and `--fail-on-drift` for CI gating; `--format json`.' Also note first-class `record --stdin` from the same change.","summary":"CHANGELOG never mentions `qualifier diff`","tags":["review","review:2026-10-01","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"AGENTS-CLI.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:18:11.952999Z","id":"80bcf97b5e43431f2e596d944cd63978c93932c675511ba9503911f12d1c0670","body":{"detail":"AGENTS-CLI.md rule 4 requires `<tool> agents <unknown-topic>` to exit with status 2 and write `<tool> agents: no such topic '<unknown>'. Available: ...`. `qualifier agents nosuch` exits 1 and prints `qualifier: no such topic 'nosuch'. Available: ...`, because src/cli/commands/agents/mod.rs:40 returns Error::Validation, which src/cli/mod.rs maps to exit 1 with prefix `qualifier:`. Lines 123-125 claim qualifier 'exercise[s] every MUST', and README.md:47 says it implements AGENTS-CLI 0.1. tests/cli_integration.rs test_agents_unknown_topic_returns_error does not assert the code. Minor: line 125 says the 'For AI agents:' group is at the top of --help, but 'Initialize:' now precedes it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":118},"end":{"line":128},"content_hash":"202f4c91f57631116d88c70b59e21a6c00d19ac06677e7fc2a96ab05d71a2c84"},"suggested_fix":"Have agents::run print the rule-4 message to stderr and `std::process::exit(2)` (or add an error variant mapped to exit 2), and assert code == 2 and the `qualifier agents:` prefix in the integration test.","summary":"Reference implementation violates AGENTS-CLI MUST rule 4: unknown topic exits 1 with the wrong message prefix","tags":["review","review:2026-10-01","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"AGENTS.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:18:11.953062Z","id":"af31e21d0bf7cb941b86aa3903528764f3e750ddb0114365ebf2ac97b66a346f","body":{"detail":"AGENTS.md 'Keeping Things in Sync' says site/js/playground.js 'contains a JavaScript scoring engine' to update when scoring logic or field names change. playground.js (header comment, lines 1-2, and section 4) is a terminal shell that runs the real qualifier CLI compiled to wasm; it has no scoring or record-format code, and scoring was removed in 0.4.0. The surface that actually drifts is site/examples/*.qual (the playground's data) and the wasm build in site/wasm/, which is gitignored and must be rebuilt for CLI changes to show up.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":42},"end":{"line":42},"content_hash":"e00c18eb12d2b464ea49d0326dcf607e0bce8a9423fc1fc0d36f7a1e84dbec9e"},"suggested_fix":"Replace the bullet with: 'site/ — the playground runs the CLI compiled to wasm over site/examples/*.qual; regenerate the examples when the record format changes and rebuild site/wasm/ for CLI changes. site/pages/*.md must match the CLI.'","summary":"AGENTS.md describes playground.js as a JavaScript scoring engine; it now only runs the wasm CLI","tags":["review","review:2026-10-01","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"METABOX.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:18:11.953100Z","id":"48f6ec2e0a895c7d3de7a40d21adb52ee06ff110666f03ec1079358fdea18acb","body":{"detail":"METABOX.md:22-23 says 'exactly eight top-level fields' and line 36-37 'All eight are present in the canonical field order', yet the same table and §3.1 make `issuer_type` optional and omitted when absent. A reader writing a validator would reject valid seven-field records.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":22},"end":{"line":37},"content_hash":"5e20acf0d66c5b4462e46a26db08c317686fef449ae12fdcbcd80860eae6d4bf"},"suggested_fix":"Say 'up to eight top-level fields (seven required, issuer_type optional)' and 'present fields appear in the canonical order'.","summary":"METABOX §1 says every record has exactly eight top-level fields, all present, while issuer_type is optional","tags":["review","review:2026-10-01","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"SPEC.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:21:38.611243Z","id":"b7bd5ce7648be33d4d2fcf55bdc2254ced76ee2e614bc2f3e68a0d79afa0d398","body":{"detail":"src/cli/mod.rs:117-126 calls config::load only to surface errors ('no command consumes Config yet'); grep for Config outside src/cli/config.rs finds no consumer. src/cli/provenance.rs reads only QUALIFIER_ISSUER, QUALIFIER_ISSUER_TYPE, QUALIFIER_SESSION and harness/VCS. SPEC.md:1196-1213 and site/pages/cli.md 'Configuration' table document .qualifier.toml, ~/.config/qualifier/config.toml and QUALIFIER_FORMAT.","kind":"comment","references":"dcef24fc5e4781e5f101194d51e856c5b59365e948811a1ad1e98e4a6120713c","summary":"confirmed: config file and QUALIFIER_FORMAT documented in SPEC 6.10 are loaded and discarded","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"SPEC.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:21:38.611254Z","id":"eb8f1d5ba252ddc79684a5a579b47a7e471a7f826e9870b1383b2fb1d2d2582b","body":{"detail":"`qualifier show src/lib.rs --line 5` -> \"error: unexpected argument '--line' found\". src/cli/commands/show.rs:24-26 documents --pretty as 'Show source context around spans (compiler-diagnostic style)'; show.rs:33-36 has an undocumented --type filter. SPEC.md:1144-1150 and site/pages/cli.md:108 say --pretty forces colored output.","kind":"comment","references":"7bc642e3d8a87d900f71723f8b2573905e646b2834dc47e15ed45618f86cbd59","summary":"confirmed: show has no --line flag and --pretty prints source context, not color","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"SPEC.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:21:38.611267Z","id":"6442816d788066865eedf40e922cedc0f5f34361cc2520354d82dd7276478d65","body":{"detail":"`qualifier --help` (0.8.0) lists init, agents, and diff. SPEC.md:901-927 §6.1 lists only record/reply/resolve/emit/show/threads/ls/praise/review/compact; the §6.x headings run 6.2 record .. 6.12 threads with no diff section; `grep -n 'qualifier diff' SPEC.md` returns nothing; init appears only at SPEC.md:1441 and agents at 1490/1499.","kind":"comment","references":"1ae0014cdd5ab2f285220d8d205a1f4bb731a546a0cce236f8670d486d45e375","summary":"confirmed: SPEC section 6 has no entry for diff, init, or agents","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"README.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:21:38.611277Z","id":"a99eaa6f8a0a8bc300d7b2d1bcc9a9c01c3386d0fc656594c78086ab8696c2dc","body":{"detail":"README.md:77-85 Inspect table lists show, threads, ls, praise, review; `grep -n diff README.md` only hits the git diff mention at line 13. `qualifier --help` lists 'diff  Show records added, resolved, or drifted since a git ref' under Inspect annotations.","kind":"comment","references":"ef6c9f07a9b19d012648a1d9cf35ff94236e3f396dfb134163592870e8fcb77b","summary":"confirmed: README Inspect table lacks qualifier diff","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"SPEC.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:21:38.611299Z","id":"fd89a1ea3c0b2581fd9e3a6b4fe8a5d2c59422a72d429c4cda702bea9d834aa6","body":{"detail":"SPEC.md:1273 says `qualifier = { version = \"0.4\", default-features = false }`; Cargo.toml:3 is 0.8.0 and src/lib.rs:5 `pub mod threads` is documented in §7 (SPEC.md ~1395). Cargo caret semantics for 0.x: \"0.4\" means >=0.4.0, <0.5.0 (https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/specifying-dependencies.html#caret-requirements). SPEC.md:1600 says 'not part of v0.3'.","kind":"comment","references":"e7a94f7b4e0d9fd5a251d067234f7a5560f2c5af662d80a9650abfebbb762cbc","summary":"confirmed: SPEC section 7 pins version 0.4 while the documented API ships in 0.8","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"SPEC.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:21:38.611308Z","id":"b2e5b970311cce8213023de8b1dee070615d8b88f7a3e1a4cbe4b241b01a640e","body":{"detail":"Public fns not in §7 (SPEC.md:1270-1400): src/qual_file.rs:46 parse_str, :74 write_all, :91 resolve_qual_path, :129 find_records_for, :140 find_annotations_for, :153 find_qual_file_for, :229 subject_name, :253 find_project_root, :274 detect_vcs; src/annotation.rs:35 Span::end_or_start, :40 Span::normalize, :48 parse_span, :106 parse_location, :487 Record::record_type, :726 check_supersession_cycles, :769 validate_supersession_targets. grep of §7 for these names finds none.","kind":"comment","references":"0911ef53b6165da15bedfb53a341b7b48475db5418b3e88e8ab46d4eb2826def","summary":"confirmed: many public library functions are missing from SPEC section 7","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"SPEC.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:21:38.611317Z","id":"146e2ad1e1fca8459074a809fa3c8934aa9e45a9d70bf2d5eb8b7028ccedf227","body":{"detail":"SPEC.md:416-418 and METABOX.md:143-144 require nested object keys sorted lexicographically (content_hash < end < start). src/annotation.rs:22-31 declares Span{start,end,content_hash} and generate_id (src/annotation.rs:546-558) serializes the struct with serde_json::to_string with no key sorting, so the hashed span is {\"start\":..,\"end\":..,\"content_hash\":..}, as stored in this repo's .qual lines (e.g. site/examples/.qual record 38fdff26). SPEC.md:449 example also shows start before end.","kind":"comment","references":"b7039ad28d4f9015640a2c84aa83ed2a6107685862d42e9fc6b8c5ee33170dc6","summary":"confirmed: MCF rule 3 requires sorted nested keys but Span hashes start, end, content_hash","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"SPEC.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:21:38.611327Z","id":"6e87ac5d369ad4cb0e400d2f7a66e0425d7ace2229e784716b2599b38da8d7a4","body":{"detail":"src/qual_file.rs:185-199 builds ignore::WalkBuilder without require_git(false) (default true: https://docs.rs/ignore/latest/ignore/struct.WalkBuilder.html#method.require_git). Scratch dir with .hg/, .gitignore 'vendor/', and vendor/.qual: `qualifier ls` -> 'vendor/v.txt (1 annotations)'; after `mv .hg .git`: 'No matching artifacts found.' SPEC.md:1514-1532 and README.md:131 state .gitignore is respected unconditionally.","kind":"comment","references":"9c7f30d62c7a9a4334ffaea04d862cbc0fc8f3f1a9247caa43285151ae2c3461","summary":"confirmed: .gitignore is ignored outside a .git repo, contrary to SPEC 10.1","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"SPEC.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:21:38.611336Z","id":"c557f7ffdd8ddc9126e2d728515a2df42b0a9f9d1e888d4f0e085b88554f0084","body":{"detail":"SPEC.md:259-261 lists flag/suggest/comment/approve/reject/attest, removed per CHANGELOG.md:181-182 ([0.4.0] Removed). SPEC.md:384 'see Appendix A' — `grep -n Appendix SPEC.md` has only that line. SPEC.md:565 'the original concern's -10 is withdrawn from scoring' though CHANGELOG.md:168-171 removed score from the format.","kind":"comment","references":"81f88ec84b199e644c33fda7e353ec00506546c418cc94856939d1b468c9fda8","summary":"confirmed: SPEC cites removed verbs, a missing Appendix A, and scoring","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"SPEC.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:21:38.611344Z","id":"307f2a0e90c89445bbe245ac6845900b3f07b9b2b91ca50957f2a9bb3201ab05","body":{"detail":"SPEC.md:1561-1590 tree lacks src/threads.rs, src/cli/provenance.rs, src/cli/targets.rs, src/cli/commands/{agents/,diff.rs,init.rs,threads.rs}, all present on disk. SPEC.md:1595 cli feature lists clap/comfy-table/figment; Cargo.toml:18 is cli = [\"dep:clap\", \"dep:comfy-table\", \"dep:figment\", \"dep:gix\", \"dep:globset\", \"dep:rand\"].","kind":"comment","references":"2e6daa85403292cd2efaf740290456ea56ad1521e935f43795a3b94b9cdf9bbd","summary":"confirmed: SPEC 11 tree and features block are stale","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"CHANGELOG.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:21:38.611353Z","id":"8bcb11f150c9457fded6f7f83cc22035fbe09f035225c00f74d8a165333c4eb9","body":{"detail":"`grep -n diff CHANGELOG.md` returns nothing. `git log --oneline -1 a6f6813` -> 'feat: qualifier diff + first-class record --stdin (#7)'; `git show a6f6813:Cargo.toml` has version = \"0.5.1\".","kind":"comment","references":"044147bd254d7992c047ad9c98bf8c5aeaf1fe908493605060ae4d5249176626","summary":"confirmed: no CHANGELOG entry mentions qualifier diff","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"AGENTS-CLI.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:21:38.611361Z","id":"ca51b734938ef601d1249a1f723edd5d30d71619d917125689b6e57c38f10aed","body":{"detail":"AGENTS-CLI.md:53-57 requires exit status 2 and the prefix '<tool> agents: no such topic'. `qualifier agents nosuch; echo $?` -> \"qualifier: no such topic 'nosuch'. Available: ...\" and exit=1; src/cli/commands/agents/mod.rs:39-43 returns Error::Validation. Correction to the finding: tests/cli_integration.rs:2456-2466 does assert the code, but asserts code == 1 and a 'qualifier:' prefix, pinning the non-conforming behavior. `qualifier --help` shows 'Initialize:' above 'For AI agents:'.","kind":"comment","references":"80bcf97b5e43431f2e596d944cd63978c93932c675511ba9503911f12d1c0670","summary":"confirmed: qualifier agents <unknown> exits 1 with 'qualifier:' prefix, violating AGENTS-CLI rule 4","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"AGENTS.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:21:38.611371Z","id":"6964280c3bc8db6bc653c52c5f827a4585aa5ce313edd242c1c4cd9bb5451937","body":{"detail":"AGENTS.md:42 calls site/js/playground.js 'a JavaScript scoring engine'. site/js/playground.js:1-2 'Runs the real qualifier CLI compiled to wasm via Emscripten'; section 4 (line 155) is the wasm layer; no score code. site/.gitignore ignores wasm/*.js and wasm/*.wasm; site/eleventy.config.js:61,156 load site/examples.","kind":"comment","references":"af31e21d0bf7cb941b86aa3903528764f3e750ddb0114365ebf2ac97b66a346f","summary":"confirmed: playground.js has no scoring engine; it runs the wasm CLI","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"METABOX.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:21:38.611379Z","id":"389127316cb1a7d3a66f72781aacf5befba20d24324d3be15b0448706997ace5","body":{"detail":"METABOX.md:22 'exactly eight top-level fields'; line 36-37 'Seven fields are required. issuer_type is optional. All eight are present in the canonical field order.' The table row 5 marks issuer_type Required: no, so the sentences contradict each other.","kind":"comment","references":"48f6ec2e0a895c7d3de7a40d21adb52ee06ff110666f03ec1079358fdea18acb","summary":"confirmed: METABOX 1 says exactly eight fields, all present, while issuer_type is optional","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
